{"availability":"available","full":"RettWilson22/gridiron-lakehouse","name":"gridiron-lakehouse","description":"Season-long fantasy football projections and weekly cheat sheet on Databricks (Lakeflow, MLflow, Unity Catalog) and Snowflake (dbt, Snowpark, streams and tasks, Streamlit)","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T00:54:21Z","updated":"2026-10-12T16:24:38Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gridiron-lakehouse.streamlit.app","topics":["data-engineering","databricks","dbt","fantasy-football","mlflow","python","snowflake","streamlit"],"demo":"https://gridiron-lakehouse.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:09.542Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:09.542Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:09.542Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:20.484Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-13T07:36:09.542Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Weekly fantasy football projections, built and backtested on Databricks and served from Snowflake.","Live demo: a public, read-only copy of the Streamlit in Snowflake app. It reads a static snapshot of the marts exported from Databricks and refreshed by hand; the Snowflake version needs a login.","Many companies run Databricks and Snowflake side by side, often owned by different teams: data engineering and machine learning on Databricks, analytics and business-facing apps on Snowflake. The hard part is the handoff between them. Here Databricks owns ingestion, transformation and the model; Snowflake owns the analytics model, the SQL-callable scoring logic, the incremental scorecard and the app. A single team starting from scratch could use one platform; the point here is working across both."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RettWilson22/gridiron-lakehouse/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fa06185dc2a88925524789c56fb2d96b02d8befc95aa9b17fc44